{
  "Question": "Consider the definite trigonometric integral: $$I = \int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \frac{\sqrt{\tan x}}{1 + 3\sin^2 x} \, dx$$ Using advanced trigonometric substitution techniques and relevant integral reduction identities (e.g., beta-gamma function relations for improper integrals of rational functions over $[0,\infty)$), what is the exact closed-form value of $I$?",
